From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] msvcrt: secure and locale string functions.

CRT string functions that were spec stubs: _strset_s, __wcsncnt,
_strerror_s (the _strerror message, truncated to the buffer), _umask_s,
_lsearch_s (with a comparison context; a missing key is appended), and the
multibyte _mbsninc_l, _mbsstr_l (matches start on character boundaries),
_mbstrnlen(_l) (EILSEQ for a lead byte without trail), _mbsset_s,
_mbsnset_s, _mbsnbset_s and _mbsncat_s with their _l forms (the string must
end within the buffer). _mbsncoll and _mbsnicoll (and _l) compare the first
count characters of each string; they were stubs in msvcrt too. msvcr80
and later, ucrtbase with its _o_ forms, msvcr120_app forwards.
